  "freshDrift": [],
  "observations": [
    "HookRuntime actual unknown callback sees only scalar/copy queries and empty ports; exact static builtin function identities receive private concrete commands. Binder maps store definitions, not World/per-game ports.",
    "Beauty keeps proposals/receipt references private in its complete owner. Source rejection precedes prepareWorld; claim precedes protection; publishAfterDeaths follows actual engine death commit. Original event and partial error prefix remains in complete owner.",
    "Ghost publication privately captures lazy world/events/day/phase sources. Expansion and per-edge group lookup precede append; events.push callee then Date.now/day/phase remain in original order.",
    "Dream matchesAlive is boolean, not readonly component return. Getter captures original World.getComponent then id evaluation; query completion precedes original-ref thunk; original receiver and same Error path are literal-tested.",
    "New narrow-hook cases cover actual function-identity binding, cross-World stock separation, unpaid thrown selection and query/ref evaluation ordering. Adapted old tests preserve domain literal stock/event/choice oracles; checks not executed by reviewer."
  ],
  "finding": {
    "id": "D-E-public-death-choice-return-component",
    "kind": "static actual source chain; no runtime counterexample executed",
    "paths": [
      "backend/src/engine/hooks/registry.ts",
      "backend/src/engine/death-resolution.ts",
      "backend/src/rulesets/death-shot-selection.ts",
      "backend/src/domain/deaths.ts",
      "backend/src/domain/night-effects.ts"
    ],
    "chain": [
      "Unknown DeathHook still receives original chooseDeathShot argument directly from invokeDeathHook",
      "DeathResolution callback returns collectDeathShot result unmodified",
      "collectDeathShot real shot returns targetScope or mapped.scope",
      "DeathShotSelection.targetScope is NightLifeScope; .life is original AliveComponent, not scalar/opaque proof"
    ],
    "minimalRisk": "A custom hook awaits choose(actorId) for a legal shot; selected.kind===shot exposes selected.targetScope.life even though HookRuntime.queries is narrow. This is an existing additional API channel, not an arbitrary externally planted object graph.",
    "suggestion": "Unknown callback choose returns only public choice/id/permit values. Exact original full selection remains in trusted static owner binding, preserving mapped current/ref and error timing for native settlement. Keep this scoped separately if Root accepts the 50-path migration as bounded delivery; do not call complete public-hook closure."
  },
